asteroids touch: no false release mid-swipe, latch the IRQ edge

A release with no UP record (all-FF buffer, frame omitting a contact, 30 ms of
errors) cut a swipe short, and the next down + real lift became a tap. Beryllium
fixed this in 0113. Also latch falling IRQ edges in the TLMM status bit and check
every 4 ms instead of 10, so a flick's first sample no longer comes late.
Boot args: sweettouchhold=MS (0 = off), sweettouchidle_ms=N, sweettouchlog=1.

